# Claiming — concurrency & qty

## Server (source of truth)

- Serialize claim writes per receipt: Postgres `FOR UPDATE` / in-memory mutex.
- `remaining = claimCapacity(item) - sum(claims.units)` where capacity is `qty` (as printed) or `qty × glassesPerPrintedUnit` (glass pour). Reject overclaim with `409 not_enough_remaining`.
- Claim `units` are always claim-grain integers (glasses or printed bottles), never fractional bottles.
- No silent optimistic commits. Clients refresh after conflict and show what’s left.
- Emit live updates (SSE + poll fallback) so other guests see decremented remaining.

## Client UX

- Only show lines with `remaining > 0`. Gone lines leave the pick list (history still shows who claimed).
- Prune the guest’s selection when live remaining hits 0; clamp queued units to max remaining.
- **Skip the qty step** when every selected line has `remaining === 1` — claim immediately with 1 unit.
- Qty stepper only when at least one selected line still has `remaining > 1`.
- Integer units only; client max = remaining at render; server re-validates.

## Do not

- Soft-hold / reserve units while someone is “thinking” unless product explicitly adds TTL holds.
- Let the qty screen appear for single-unit lines.
- Trust client remaining without the server check.
